# Pre-push intentionally does NOT re-run the heavy gate suite.
#
# The full gate set (test:coverage, build, and the rest) is run ONCE in the
# foreground BEFORE each commit — see the CI-gates and incremental-commit
# rules — and authoritatively in CI. Re-running coverage + build on every push
# only duplicated that CPU locally, which is wasteful on constrained machines.
#
# Verification happens at/before commit time (pre-commit lint-staged + typecheck
# + the foreground gate run) and again in CI. This hook is a deliberate no-op.
exit 0
